<title>JAPAN: High-tech shares up in Tokyo on recovery hopes.</title>
<headline>High-tech shares up in Tokyo on recovery hopes.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Semiconductor-related issues were higher in Wednesday morning trade, gathering the attention of investors due to hopes that the sector is headed for a recovery, brokers said.</p>
<p>They said interest in the shares was contributing the Nikkei average's rebound.</p>
<p>At 0133 GMT, Nikon Corp was up 40 yen at 1,600, in a trade of 1.851 million shares, the seventh largest percentage gainer on the Tokyo bourse. Advantest Corp surged 120 yen to 6,200 yen.</p>
<p>Tokyo Electron Ltd was up 100 yen at 3,970 yen.</p>
</text>
